@@part Part I — Understanding IDEs

# What Is an IDE?

## A first look

An **IDE** is a program that helps you write programs. This sentence is a test of *italic*, **bold** and `inline code`.

{{fig:ide-vs-editor|An editor is the middle of the onion. An IDE wraps more tools around it.}}

::: why Why does it matter?
Because every layer saves you time. Without it you would do each step by hand.
:::

```c run
#include <stdio.h>
int main(void) {
    printf("Hello, NOVA!\n");
    return 0;
}
```

| Word | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| IDE | Integrated Development Environment |
| LSP | Language Server Protocol |

{{img:shot-run.png|The NOVA window after pressing Run.}}

